{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:100729","published":"2026-11-21T06:02:09.442856Z","modified":"2026-11-21T06:30:03.087624297Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-64375","CVE-2026-64549","CVE-2026-68326","CVE-2026-68470","CVE-2026-74488","CVE-2026-74493","CVE-2026-74631","CVE-2026-74637","CVE-2026-89965","CVE-2026-90057","CVE-2026-97528","CVE-2026-98323","CVE-2026-99064"],"summary":"Important: kernel-rt security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: proc: protect ptrace_may_access() with exec_update_lock (FD links) (CVE-2026-64375)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)\n\n* kernel: wifi: mwifiex: bound uAP association event IEs to the event buffer (CVE-2026-68326)\n\n* kernel: wifi: mac80211: validate extension-frame layout before RX (CVE-2026-68470)\n\n* kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)\n\n* kernel: wifi: mwifiex: use the subframe length when parsing A-MSDU TDLS frames (CVE-2026-74488)\n\n* kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n\n* kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)\n\n* kernel: nvdimm/btt: reject an arena whose nfree is below the lane count (CVE-2026-89965)\n\n* kernel: slip: remove slip_hangup() to fix use-after-free in slip_receive_buf() (CVE-2026-90057)\n\n* kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/siw: Bound fragmented header copies by the remaining length (CVE-2026-98323)\n\n* kernel: cipso: adjust cached option offsets when removing CIPSO (CVE-2026-99064)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [Rocky Linux-8] The slab cache entries for gfs2 and dlm grow very large for gfs2 filesystems (JIRA:Rocky Linux-220529)\n\n* XFS NULL pointer dereference in xfs_inode_mark_reclaimable due to race in xfs_free_perag during umount (JIRA:Rocky Linux-247835)\n\n* kprobe/ftrace: use-after-free and panic after ftrace_kill(), needs backport of 1a7d0890dd4a and e113f0b46d19 (JIRA:Rocky Linux-284885)\n\n* Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-286158)\n\n* Backport CVEs from v7.2 [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-300371)\n\n* Fix crasher in gss_unwrap_resp_integ() (JIRA:Rocky Linux-309171)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug-devel","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug-devel?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-core?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug-core?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debuginfo-common-x86_64","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debuginfo-common-x86_64?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.187.1.rt7.528.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100729.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug-kvm","